 2]}, {"type": "paragraph", "snippet": "To qualify for paid maternity leave under the Code on Social Security / Maternity Benefit Act, an employee must meet these conditions:", "reference_indexes": [2]}, {"type": "list", "list": [{"snippet": "Work in an establishment with 10 or more employees (in the public or private sector)."}, {"snippet": "Have worked for the employer for at least 80 days in the 12 months immediately preceding the date of expected delivery."}, {"snippet": "Salary: The employer (or the Employee State Insurance Corporation, if eligible) pays 100% of the employee's average daily wage during the leave period .", "reference_indexes": [2]}, {"snippet": "Additional Provisions: Employers must also provide nursing breaks until the child is 15 months old and mandatory crèche facilities for establishments with 50 or more employees."}], "reference_indexes": [2, 3, 2]}, {"type": "paragraph", "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"}, {"type": "list", "list": [{"snippet": "Is this for the private sector or civil service/government?"}, {"snippet": "Are you checking eligibility for a specific situation (such as adoption or third child)?"}]}], "references": [{"index": 0, "title": "India Maternity Leave Laws: 26 Weeks Paid Leave ... - LinkedIn", "link": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sapna-pandey-08582b105_maternitybenefitact-indianlabourlaw-hrcompliance-activity-7420426029191684096-CoN0", "snippet": "Eligible women must have worked for at least 80 days in the 12 months preceding delivery in establishments with 10 or more employees. # Key_Aspects_of_Maternity_Le...", "source": "LinkedIn", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://www.linkedin.com&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL", "thumbnail": "https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQgJIIoFmrlbi-wxuj7tWJ4dW_xhKgsQGrU8H1rYjrrfeOhGCnaHUcY2OfQQRWZJwFp4lD0zvf4EOy31_TYPLQ4JWg"}, {"index": 1, "title": "Maternity Law in India | Employer Compliance Guide | 2025", "link": "https://vishaalconsultancy.com/maternity-law-in-india/", "snippet": "How Long Is Maternity Leave in India? Here's the breakdown: 26 weeks paid leave for the first and second child (8 weeks pre-delivery, 18 weeks post-delivery) 12 we...", "source": "Vishaal Consultancy Services", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://vishaalconsultancy.com&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL", "thumbnail": "https://encrypted-tbn3.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQ-q4yLrUSBcddLp-ROeV6N35alzQe73raDyURw18z1R7BbkyBHA0JrYJhtnE9d35mgu5mFDcxRqi0oxVfvgr0f7eLbr362Sa9Qa5fl"}, {"index": 2, "title": "Maternity Leave in India 2026: Rules & Pay - Wisemonk", "link": "https://www.wisemonk.io/blogs/maternity-leave-in-india", "snippet": "* Maternity leave in India is 26 weeks of fully paid leave for the first two children and 12 weeks from the third, under Chapter VI of the Code on Social Security,", "source": "Wisemonk", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://www.wisemonk.io&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL", "thumbnail": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcSITsHHg6iUK1c9PNAMyk0NqOMrgZKuUb4CVHtWxuPpZ1ytIHEdXbQj1jG_7_JSk5WC6awW0wpFDdQXpASvKXKkRK3xhUuKv8p_eYl8"}, {"index": 3, "title": "Maternity Leave in India: What Are the Rules?", "link": "https://www.sbigeneral.in/blog/health-insurance/health-gi-simplified/maternity-leave-in-india-what-are-the-rules", "snippet": "FAQs What are the criteria for maternity leave eligibility? Here are some of the criteria for qualifying for maternity leave: Minimum 80 working days with the empl...", "source": "SBI General Insurance", "source_icon": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/faviconV2?url=https://www.sbigeneral.in&client=AIM&size=128&type=FAVICON&fallback_opts=TYPE,SIZE,URL", "thumbnail": "https://encrypted-tbn2.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQKZMLFXmSPcatc2BXAxlYUkkALMj6xYyjYpxrBZXxWxd9SJxpXOtC6Fy5m